# Keys format (WEWIN) — Key 9 is default

Canonical keys file = **`Key N.docx`** style (see `templates/canonical-keys.md`):

- Headings: `Listening` / `Reading` (one file may contain both)
- Optional: `Section 1–4`, `Passage 1–3`
- Answers: **`N. answer`** per line (or Word table cells with the same text)
- Reading: `TRUE` / `FALSE` / `NOT GIVEN` (also `T`/`F`/`NGV`)
- **No screenshots** — parser cannot OCR images

Import path:
1. Extract keys text (+ Word tables → TSV)
2. `parseKeysCanonical()` / `normalizeKeysToCanonical()` rewrites odd layouts into Key 9 shape
3. Merge into Listening/Reading questions

When the user sends a non-conforming keys file, **normalize automatically** (do not ask them to retype if text is recoverable). If keys are image-only, report `KEYS_IMAGE_ONLY` and request Key-9 text/table.
